1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,200
Most VR productivity apps throw massive 2D screens across your entire room, forcing you to stand up or reach into the void.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:16,200
Meet SynapseDesk AI: the hands-first, seated autonomous spatial workspace built exclusively for Meta Quest.

3
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:23,500
Engineered strictly for the Airplane Seat Test, every interaction stays inside a comfortable two-foot radius arc.

4
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:30,500
Requiring zero controllers, we simply poke the Horizon Store Launch sprint on the Cognitive Capture panel with our index finger.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,800
The Synapse Core agent decomposes our ambition into prioritized 3D physical task prisms. Users pinch and manipulate nodes with bare hands.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:49,200
Tapping the crystalline core triggers real-time force-directed auto-clustering, snapping chaotic nodes into an ergonomic field-of-view corridor.

7
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:57,200
For rapid daily momentum, the One Bus Stop mode provides a five-minute seated focus sprint with procedural Web Audio feedback.

8
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:04,800
We complete our tasks, observe our cognitive load balance in real time, and export our structured action plan.

9
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:11,500
100 percent hands-first, strictly seated, and locked at 60 FPS.

10
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:19,200
SynapseDesk AI: built with the official Meta Immersive Web SDK for the Meta VR Start Developer Competition 2026.
